// src/kernel/core/fs/pdxfs/probe.pdx -- R52.M5-004 (#1706)
//
// PDXFS-ON-BLOCK v1 -- VOLUME DISCOVERY (iterate every live KIND_BLKDEV,
// read + validate LBA 0, register in the volume registry).
//
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Scope
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//
// Per design/filesystem/r52-implementation-plan.md §2.5 step 4 (#1706)
// and design/filesystem/volume-fs-substrate.md §3.1: "At boot, after
// the R51 driver family has registered its devices, ... `probe.pdx`
// iterates the kernel's list of live `KIND_BLOCK_DEVICE` capabilities:
// (1) BD_OP_QUERY; (2) BD_OP_READ_LBA(0); (3) magic/version check;
// (4) sig verify; (5) register into KIND_VOLUME + the volume
// registry." The implementation plan's own narrower scope line for
// #1706 covers steps (2)/(3)/(5): "iterate every live KIND_BLKDEV,
// BD_OP_READ_LBA(0), magic gate, register" -- it drops step (1)
// (BD_OP_QUERY, no check here needs the device's own reported LBA
// count / block size -- `sb_read` already validates `block_size` from
// the SUPERBLOCK's own field) and step (4) (sig verify, deferred to
// mount-time per #1707/§6.4 -- see the design-doc-gap note in
// volume_registry.pdx's own header, restated here since it governs
// this file's behaviour equally).
//
// Two building blocks compose this file's whole job:
//   - `sb_read` (superblock_read.pdx, #1686) does the BDEV_OP_READ_LBA
//     + magic/version/block_size/reserved validation (steps 2-3).
//   - `volume_registry_register` (volume_registry.pdx, #1706, this
//     same milestone) does the uuid-indexed idempotent registration +
//     KIND_VOLUME row population (step 5).
// This file's own code is exactly the device ENUMERATION loop plus the
// glue between those two calls -- it holds no storage of its own
// beyond a small observability counter block.
//
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Device enumeration
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//
// There is no existing "walk every live cap of kind K" primitive in
// this kernel (grep audit 2026-08-23: no `cap_scan_kind` / `for_each_
// live` helper anywhere under `src/kernel/core/`). `probe_all_bdevs`
// therefore scans the raw 256-slot `cap_table` directly, exactly
// mirroring `kind_volume.pdx`'s own `volume_row_of_slot` addressing
// idiom (`cap_table + slot*24`, stride = shl 3 + shl 4, kind word at
// `+0`) -- the same pattern already proven correct and already
// confined to no single owner (cap_table itself is read-only from
// this walker's perspective; it never writes an entry). `KIND_BLKDEV`
// (0x42, cap/blkdev_cap.pdx) is re-stated here as a literal per this
// codebase's "constants are re-declared, not cross-file-imported by
// name" convention (see superblock.pdx's own header note on the same
// point).
//
// `cap_invoke`'s own rights/bounds gates (reached transitively through
// `sb_read`) are the only access control exercised here -- this
// walker holds no rights argument of its own and trusts every live
// `KIND_BLKDEV` slot it finds to be readable by boot-time kernel code,
// matching every prior R52.M2-M4 caller's posture (mkfs.pdx,
// superblock_read.pdx, allocator.pdx, inode_table.pdx all call
// `cap_invoke` the same way with no separate rights plumbing).
//
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Failure modes are non-fatal (design/filesystem/volume-fs-substrate.md §3.1)
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//
// "A device whose block 0 is not a PdxFS-on-block v1 superblock is
// skipped, not an error." `probe_one_bdev` implements this by
// forwarding `sb_read`'s own return verbatim on failure (one of
// `PDXB_SB_MAGIC_BAD`/`_VERSION_BAD`/`_BLOCK_SIZE_BAD`/
// `_RESERVED_NONZERO`/`PDXB_SB_READ_BDEV_ERR`, all < 2^32) rather than
// treating it as fatal; `probe_all_bdevs` simply does not count that
// slot toward its returned "volumes registered" total and continues
// scanning. The substrate doc's own chatter-line suggestion ("PDXFS
// PROBE BAD_MAGIC lba=0 dev=<cap>" via dmesg) is FLAGGED, not
// implemented, here: no FS-layer module landed so far in R52
// (mkfs.pdx, allocator.pdx, inode_table.pdx, journal_ondisk.pdx) calls
// any chatter/klog print helper from inside its own body -- every one
// of them returns a typed code and leaves printing to the boot-witness
// layer that calls it (`src/kernel/boot/witness/r52_platform.pdx`,
// still unwritten -- the M5 witness lands at #1708, not here). This
// file follows that same precedent rather than introducing the first
// FS-layer chatter call site out of scope.
//
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Distinguishing a real pointer from a sentinel error code
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//
// `sb_read` returns either `&_sb_read_buf` (a real kernel address) or
// one of five sentinels in `0xFFFFED00..0xFFFFED08`. Every real kernel
// address in this build is `>= KERNEL_VMA_BASE` (`0xFFFF800000000000`,
// `src/kernel/link.ld`, also staged as an immediate the same way in
// `kernel_main.pdx`), which is vastly larger than any `0xFFFFEDxx`
// sentinel (< 2^32). `probe_one_bdev` stages `0xFFFF800000000000` into
// a register and compares (`cmp rax, r10; jb <sentinel>`) rather than
// comparing against a small threshold directly -- both operands are
// full 64-bit registers, so there is no `cmp reg, imm32`
// sign-extension hazard (the hazard this codebase flags repeatedly
// applies only to immediate operands, not register-register compares).
// `probe_one_bdev`'s OWN return value mixes the same two domains (a
// `row_id` 0..15 from a successful registration, or one of `sb_read`'s
// sentinels, or `volume_registry_insert`'s `VOL_TAIL_BAD_ARG`/
// `VOL_REGISTRY_FULL`, both >= `0xFFFFED00`) -- `probe_all_bdevs`
// disambiguates the same way every other R52 module does (`inode_
// alloc_fresh`, `volume_tail_alloc`, ...): `cmp rax, 16; jae <not a
// row_id>` (row ids are 0..15; every failure sentinel this file can
// produce is far larger).
//
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Arity discipline (design/filesystem/r52-implementation-plan.md §5.1)
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//
// §5.1's table: "probe.pdx | probe_one_bdev | arity 1. Fine." Landed
// exactly as `probe_one_bdev(bdev_cap) -> u64`, arity 1. `probe_all_
// bdevs` is arity 0 (no caller-supplied state -- it owns its own loop
// index and count locally).
//
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Register discipline
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//
// `probe_one_bdev` issues four nested calls in its success path
// (`sb_read`, `sb_uuid_lo`, `sb_uuid_hi`, `volume_registry_register`)
// and needs `bdev_slot`/`sb_ptr`/`uuid_lo`/`uuid_hi` (4 values) alive
// across them; rather than an even 4-push + `sub rsp,8` pad, it takes
// the uniform 5-push shape `sb_read` itself uses (rbx/r12/r13/r14/r15,
// with r15 unused but pushed for pattern uniformity -- matching sb_
// read's own documented precedent), landing rsp%16==0 with no pad
// (odd count). `probe_all_bdevs` needs only two values (count, slot
// index) alive across its one nested call (`probe_one_bdev`): 2-push
// prologue (rbx=count, r12=slot) + `sub rsp,8` pad (even count), per
// journal_ondisk.pdx's documented rule.
//
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// mov_b / no-test / label-prefix discipline
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//
// No byte-granularity access in this file (every field touched is a
// whole qword: cap_table's kind word, sb_ptr, uuid halves, slot
// index). No `test` instruction; every branch uses `cmp reg, imm` /
// `cmp reg, reg` + `je`/`jne`/`jb`/`jae`. Every label is prefixed
// `pbob_` (`probe_one_bdev`) or `pbab_` (`probe_all_bdevs`) -- grep
// audit 2026-08-23: no hits anywhere in `src/kernel/` for either
// prefix. Stats helpers are named `pdxfs_probe_note`/`pdxfs_probe_stat`
// (not the bare `probe_note`/`probe_stat` several unrelated
// `core/drivers/*/probe.pdx` files might plausibly want for
// themselves -- this file's own `module Probe = structure { ... }`
// name is itself reused across `core/drivers/{ahci,nvme,vmd,xhci,
// e1000e}/probe.pdx` with no collision, since module names are not
// linked symbols; the `pub let` function/data symbols inside a module
// ARE globally linked, so this file's own exports use the more
// specific `pdxfs_probe_*` / `probe_one_bdev` / `probe_all_bdevs`
// names instead of anything bare-`probe_*`).
//
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Failure taxonomy
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//
// This file declares no NEW failure codes. `probe_one_bdev` forwards,
// verbatim, whatever `sb_read` or `volume_registry_register` returns
// (superblock_read.pdx's `PDXB_SB_READ_BDEV_ERR` 0xFFFFED08;
// superblock.pdx's `PDXB_SB_MAGIC_BAD`/`_VERSION_BAD`/`_BLOCK_SIZE_BAD`/
// `_RESERVED_NONZERO` 0xFFFFED00..03; kind_volume.pdx's
// `VOL_TAIL_BAD_ARG` 0xFFFFED22 / `VOL_REGISTRY_FULL` 0xFFFFED25).

module Probe = structure {

  // ============================================================================
  // Stats. 0 = SCANNED (every live KIND_BLKDEV slot seen), 1 = REGISTERED
  // (probe_one_bdev returned a row_id), 2 = SKIPPED (sb_read/registry
  // returned a sentinel -- non-fatal per module header).
  //
  // R53.M5-005 (#1758): family-aware scan counters landed at indices 3
  // (NVMe: family byte in {0, 1}, cap/blkdev_cap.pdx BLK_CAP_FAMILY_
  // LEGACY_NVME/BLK_CAP_FAMILY_NVME) and 4 (AHCI: family byte 2,
  // BLK_CAP_FAMILY_AHCI). Both are bumped in probe_all_bdevs's walk
  // BEFORE the probe_one_bdev call, right after the family byte is
  // extracted from cap_table[slot] + 16 (target_ptr bits [23:16] per
  // blkdev_cap.pdx §Family bytes / cap_handler_blkdev.pdx's family
  // demux). The composite PBP_ST_SCANNED counter at index 0 stays as
  // it was -- bumped inside probe_one_bdev's entry, matching every
  // existing caller's expectation. Growing the stats array from
  // [u64;4] to [u64;8] leaves index 5..7 reserved for any future
  // family split (per the same family-tag registry consumers today).
  // ============================================================================

  pub let mut _pdxfs_probe_stats : [u64; 8] = uninit @align(64)

  pub let PBP_ST_SCANNED       : u64 = 0
  pub let PBP_ST_REGISTERED    : u64 = 1
  pub let PBP_ST_SKIPPED       : u64 = 2
  pub let PBP_ST_SCANNED_NVME  : u64 = 3
  pub let PBP_ST_SCANNED_AHCI  : u64 = 4
  pub let PBP_ST_MAX           : u64 = 8

  // ============================================================================
  // Fingerprint strings emitted at the two probe_one_bdev exit paths.
  // Output-strip-clean per design/policy/output-provenance-strip.md (no
  // round/milestone/issue reference in either string). Length count
  // includes the trailing "\n\0" pair. Consumed by tests/r17/shell-
  // shutdown.golden's subsequence check plus every future live-arm
  // golden that pins the OK line.
  // ============================================================================

  pub let pdxb_probe_ok_msg   : [u8; 15] = "PDXB PROBE OK\n\0"
  pub let pdxb_probe_skip_msg : [u8; 17] = "PDXB PROBE SKIP\n\0"

  pub let pdxfs_probe_note : (u64) -> () !{mem} @{} =
    fn (which: u64) -> unsafe {
      effects: {mem}, capabilities: {},
      justification: "R52.M5-004 (#1706) + R53.M5-005 (#1758): bounded increment; out-of-range no-op. Leaf, mirrors kind_volume.pdx's volume_note / volume_registry.pdx's volume_registry_note. Bound raised from 4 to 8 at R53.M5-005 (#1758) alongside the two new family-aware indices (PBP_ST_SCANNED_NVME=3, PBP_ST_SCANNED_AHCI=4) that probe_all_bdevs now bumps once per KIND_BLKDEV slot seen -- the array itself was grown to [u64;8] under the same change.",
      block: {
        cmp rdi, 8;
        jae pbnt_out;
        lea r10, [rip + _pdxfs_probe_stats];
        mov rax, [r10 + rdi * 8];
        add rax, 1;
        mov [r10 + rdi * 8], rax;
      pbnt_out:
        ret
      }
    }

  pub let pdxfs_probe_stat : (u64) -> u64 !{mem} @{} =
    fn (which: u64) -> unsafe {
      effects: {mem}, capabilities: {},
      justification: "R52.M5-004 (#1706) + R53.M5-005 (#1758): bounded read; out-of-range returns 0. Bound raised from 4 to 8 at R53.M5-005 (#1758) alongside the family-aware indices PBP_ST_SCANNED_NVME (3) and PBP_ST_SCANNED_AHCI (4) that pdxb_ahci_probe.pdx's boot witness (#1758) reads to prove an AHCI-family KIND_BLKDEV slot reached the probe walker.",
      block: {
        cmp rdi, 8;
        jae pbst_zero;
        lea r10, [rip + _pdxfs_probe_stats];
        mov rax, [r10 + rdi * 8];
        ret;
      pbst_zero:
        xor rax, rax;
        ret
      }
    }

  // ==========================================================================
  // probe_one_bdev(bdev_slot) -> row_id | err
  //
  // Reads + validates LBA 0 of ONE bdev cap slot, then registers it.
  // Non-fatal on any validation failure -- returns the failing
  // sentinel verbatim, does not panic or print. 5-push prologue
  // (rbx=bdev_slot, r12=sb_ptr, r13=uuid_lo, r14=uuid_hi, r15 unused)
  // lands rsp%16==0 (odd count, no pad), mirroring sb_read's own
  // 5-push shape.
  // ==========================================================================
  pub let probe_one_bdev : (u64) -> u64 !{mem, sysreg} @{cap} =
    fn (bdev_slot: u64) -> unsafe {
      effects: {mem, sysreg},
      capabilities: {cap},
      justification: "R52.M5-004 (#1706) + R53.M3-005 fingerprint hook: validate + register one KIND_BLKDEV slot's LBA 0. 5-push prologue (rbx/r12/r13/r14/r15) lands rsp%16==0 (odd count, sb_read's own shape); r15 unused, pushed for pattern uniformity. Body: rbx=bdev_slot(rdi). rdi=rbx; call sb_read -> rax = sb_ptr or a <2^32 sentinel (PDXB_SB_READ_BDEV_ERR/_MAGIC_BAD/_VERSION_BAD/_BLOCK_SIZE_BAD/_RESERVED_NONZERO). Distinguish real pointer from sentinel: mov r10,0xFFFF800000000000 (KERNEL_VMA_BASE, link.ld); cmp rax,r10; jb pbob_tally (sentinel -- non-fatal skip, forward rax verbatim through the tally). Else r12=rax(sb_ptr). rdi=r12; call sb_uuid_lo; r13=rax. rdi=r12; call sb_uuid_hi; r14=rax. rdi=rbx(device_slot), rsi=r13(uuid_lo), rdx=r14(uuid_hi), rcx=r12(sb_ptr); call volume_registry_register -- forwards its row_id-or-error verbatim into rax. Stats + fingerprint: bump PBP_ST_SCANNED once at entry (before the sentinel check, since every slot reaching this function was a live KIND_BLKDEV the caller counted); at pbob_tally, spill rax through rbx (bdev_slot is dead by this point; the callee-save rbx survives both the pdxfs_probe_note leaf AND the klog_s1 nested emit whereas r10 would be clobbered by either), bump PBP_ST_REGISTERED + emit 'PDXB PROBE OK' via klog_s1 on rax<16, else bump PBP_ST_SKIPPED + emit 'PDXB PROBE SKIP' -- both fingerprints are output-strip-clean per design/policy/output-provenance-strip.md. The rbx spill also closes a latent bug in the pre-hook code where r10 (caller-save, in fact clobbered by pdxfs_probe_note's own `lea r10, [rip + _pdxfs_probe_stats]`) was used for the same save/restore; the pre-hook return value happened to still pass every caller's `cmp rax, 16` test purely because the clobbered value was also >= 16. Reserved labels: pbob_.",
      block: {
        push rbx;
        push r12;
        push r13;
        push r14;
        push r15;

        mov rbx, rdi;                    // bdev_slot

        mov rdi, 0;                      // PBP_ST_SCANNED
        call pdxfs_probe_note;

        mov rdi, rbx;
        call sb_read;

        mov r10, 0xFFFF800000000000;     // KERNEL_VMA_BASE
        cmp rax, r10;
        jb pbob_tally;                   // sentinel: non-fatal skip, rax already set

        mov r12, rax;                    // sb_ptr

        // R53.M5-003 (#1756) sig-verify observability hook.
        // Runs sig_hash_verify_stub (sig_verify.pdx #1701) against the
        // just-read superblock and its stored sig_key_hash field.  The
        // stub is fail-closed today (always returns
        // INODE_TAIL_HASH_MISMATCH 0xFFFFED1C -- BLAKE3-hash-32 is a
        // confirmed paideia-as gap, RELEASE-NOTES-v0.20.md), so a
        // mismatch here does NOT (yet) block registration -- blocking
        // would break every LIVE-arm witness whose disk carries a
        // signed-but-unverifiable superblock.  The audit line fires
        // regardless so the ring records the refusal-shape.  A follow-
        // up flips this from OBSERVATION to REFUSAL by inserting
        // `jmp pbob_tally` after audit_emit (rax already carries a
        // valid skip sentinel per the pbob_tally row_id/sentinel
        // disambiguation, cmp rax,16;jae pbob_skipped).
        //
        // audit_emit(kind=0, slot=bdev_slot, evt=AUD_VOLUME_SIG_MISMATCH
        // (evt ordinal from sibling #1754's AUD_* union widening -- 15
        // in the plan-doc's own order after AUD_MOUNT=13/AUD_UMOUNT=14),
        // at=0, result=0, payload_lo=sig_key_hash_hi -- last qword of
        // the 32-byte BLAKE3 fingerprint at sb+128+24 per superblock_
        // fmt.pdx's PDXB_SB_SIG_KEY_HASH_OFFSET/_LEN).  Return value
        // discarded per audit-is-best-effort convention (matches every
        // other audit_emit call site; if #1754 has not landed,
        // aud_ev_valid rejects with AUD_ERR_BAD_EVT and no record
        // enters the ring but the call site is wired for future
        // activation).  Register plan: sig_hash_verify_stub is a leaf
        // and does not touch r12 (sb_ptr) or rbx (bdev_slot); audit_
        // emit preserves all callee-save regs (r12/rbx included per
        // its own 5-push prologue), so sb_uuid_lo below still sees
        // r12=sb_ptr on the fall-through path.  Substrate posture: no
        // live KIND_BLKDEV means probe_one_bdev is not called at all,
        // so this hook fires only on a LIVE arm (real disk attached
        // OR a test synthesizes a KIND_BLKDEV cap).
        mov rdi, r12;                    // sig_block_ptr = sb_ptr
        mov rsi, r12;
        add rsi, 128;                    // sig_hash_ptr = &sb[+128] (PDXB_SB_SIG_KEY_HASH_OFFSET)
        call sig_hash_verify_stub;
        cmp rax, 0;
        je  pbob_sig_ok;
        xor rdi, rdi;                    // kind = 0 (non-cap event)
        mov rsi, rbx;                    // slot = bdev_slot
        mov rdx, 15;                     // evt = AUD_VOLUME_SIG_MISMATCH (#1754)
        xor rcx, rcx;                    // at = 0
        xor r8,  r8;                     // result = 0
        mov r9, [r12 + 152];             // payload_lo = sig_key_hash_hi ([sb+128+24])
        call audit_emit;                 // best-effort; rax discarded
      pbob_sig_ok:

        mov rdi, r12;
        call sb_uuid_lo;
        mov r13, rax;

        mov rdi, r12;
        call sb_uuid_hi;
        mov r14, rax;

        mov rdi, rbx;                    // device_slot
        mov rsi, r13;                    // uuid_lo
        mov rdx, r14;                    // uuid_hi
        mov rcx, r12;                    // sb_ptr
        call volume_registry_register;

      pbob_tally:
        mov r10, 16;
        cmp rax, r10;
        jae pbob_skipped;
        mov rbx, rax;                    // save row_id in rbx (callee-save,
                                         // survives note+klog; bdev_slot dead)
        mov rdi, 1;                      // PBP_ST_REGISTERED
        call pdxfs_probe_note;
        mov rdi, 3;                      // LEVEL_INFO
        lea rsi, [rip + SUBSYS_BOOT];
        lea rdx, [rip + pdxb_probe_ok_msg];
        call klog_s1;
        mov rax, rbx;                    // restore row_id
        jmp pbob_out;

      pbob_skipped:
        mov rbx, rax;                    // save sentinel in rbx (callee-save)
        mov rdi, 2;                      // PBP_ST_SKIPPED
        call pdxfs_probe_note;
        mov rdi, 3;                      // LEVEL_INFO
        lea rsi, [rip + SUBSYS_BOOT];
        lea rdx, [rip + pdxb_probe_skip_msg];
        call klog_s1;
        mov rax, rbx;                    // restore sentinel

      pbob_out:
        pop r15;
        pop r14;
        pop r13;
        pop r12;
        pop rbx;
        ret
      }
    }

  // ==========================================================================
  // probe_all_bdevs() -> u64
  //   Returns the count of KIND_BLKDEV slots that were successfully
  //   registered (row_id < 16) into the volume registry. Scans the raw
  //   256-slot cap_table directly (no "for each live cap of kind K"
  //   primitive exists yet -- see module header). 2-push prologue
  //   (rbx=count, r12=slot) + sub rsp,8 pad (even count).
  // ==========================================================================
  pub let probe_all_bdevs : () -> u64 !{mem, sysreg} @{cap} =
    fn () -> unsafe {
      effects: {mem, sysreg},
      capabilities: {cap},
      justification: "R52.M5-004 (#1706) + R53.M5-005 (#1758): top-level boot-time device walker. 2-push prologue (rbx=count, r12=slot) + sub rsp,8 pad lands rsp%16==0 (even count). Body: xor rbx,rbx (count=0); xor r12,r12 (slot=0). Loop pbab_top: cmp r12,256; jae pbab_done. Address &cap_table[slot]: mov rax,cap_table; mov r8,r12; shl r8,3; mov r9,r12; shl r9,4; add r8,r9; add rax,r8 -- identical stride arithmetic (slot*24) to kind_volume.pdx's volume_row_of_slot. mov r10,[rax+0] (kind word); cmp r10,0x42 (KIND_BLKDEV, cap/blkdev_cap.pdx, re-stated as a literal per this codebase's constant-restatement convention); jne pbab_next (not a blkdev slot). R53.M5-005 (#1758) family-byte demux: mov r10,[rax+16] (target_ptr, cap/mint.pdx L126 layout); shr r10,16; and r10,0xFF (family byte per blkdev_cap.pdx §Family bytes, target_ptr[23:16], BLK_CAP_FAMILY_LEGACY_NVME=0 / _NVME=1 / _AHCI=2). Family split via cmp r10,2 (AHCI, restated as a literal per this codebase's constant convention; the two-source-of-truth risk is that blkdev_cap.pdx's BLK_CAP_FAMILY_AHCI could move -- the same risk kind_ahci_port.pdx's AHCIP_FAMILY_AHCI already accepts for its own inline copy per that file's L197 justification): family==2 -> bump PBP_ST_SCANNED_AHCI (index 4); else -> bump PBP_ST_SCANNED_NVME (index 3, covering both LEGACY_NVME=0 and NVME=1 since the probe walker itself is family-agnostic beyond the AHCI vs NVMe split -- any non-AHCI KIND_BLKDEV reaches sb_read via the family-agnostic BDEV_OP_READ_LBA seam, and cap_handler_blkdev's own family demux handles the NVMe subsplit). Both counter bumps go through pdxfs_probe_note (leaf, no rsp adjust needed inside this even-count prologue). rdi=r12; call probe_one_bdev. mov r10,16; cmp rax,r10; jae pbab_next (sentinel, not a row_id -- do not count). add rbx,1. pbab_next: add r12,1; jmp pbab_top. pbab_done: mov rax,rbx. Reserved labels: pbab_.",
      block: {
        push rbx;
        push r12;
        sub rsp, 8;

        xor rbx, rbx;                    // count
        xor r12, r12;                    // slot

      pbab_top:
        cmp r12, 256;
        jae pbab_done;

        mov rax, cap_table;
        mov r8, r12;
        shl r8, 3;
        mov r9, r12;
        shl r9, 4;
        add r8, r9;
        add rax, r8;

        mov r10, [rax + 0];
        cmp r10, 0x42;                   // KIND_BLKDEV
        jne pbab_next;

        // R53.M5-005 (#1758): family-byte demux BEFORE the probe call.
        // target_ptr layout per cap/mint.pdx L126: kind at +0, rights
        // at +8, target_ptr at +16. Family byte lives in target_ptr
        // [23:16] per blkdev_cap.pdx §Family bytes (LEGACY_NVME=0,
        // NVME=1, AHCI=2). rax still holds &cap_table[slot] from the
        // address computation above; reuse it.
        mov r10, [rax + 16];             // target_ptr
        shr r10, 16;
        and r10, 0xFF;                   // family byte in low 8 bits
        cmp r10, 2;                      // BLK_CAP_FAMILY_AHCI
        je  pbab_fam_ahci;

        // family in {0, 1} = NVMe / legacy NVMe.
        mov rdi, 3;                      // PBP_ST_SCANNED_NVME
        call pdxfs_probe_note;
        jmp pbab_after_fam;

      pbab_fam_ahci:
        mov rdi, 4;                      // PBP_ST_SCANNED_AHCI
        call pdxfs_probe_note;

      pbab_after_fam:
        mov rdi, r12;
        call probe_one_bdev;

        mov r10, 16;
        cmp rax, r10;
        jae pbab_next;

        add rbx, 1;

      pbab_next:
        add r12, 1;
        jmp pbab_top;

      pbab_done:
        mov rax, rbx;

        add rsp, 8;
        pop r12;
        pop rbx;
        ret
      }
    }

  // ==========================================================================
  // pdxb_volume_probe_all_bdev() -> u64
  //
  // R53.M3-002 (#1743): consumer-facing alias for `probe_all_bdevs`,
  // used by kernel_main.pdx's boot-time volume-probe wire-in per
  // design/tooling/volume-lifecycle-mechanism.md §4.1 (the design
  // document names the entry point `pdxb_volume_probe_all_bdev`;
  // this file's own internal walker is `probe_all_bdevs`).
  //
  // Thin forward: same signature, same behaviour -- returns rax
  // (count of KIND_BLKDEV slots that were successfully registered
  // into the volume registry) verbatim. Substrate posture: when no
  // KIND_BLKDEV caps have been minted (no nvme_probe / ahci_probe
  // wire-in upstream yet on the current -kernel/BIOS boot path),
  // probe_all_bdevs scans 256 cap_table slots, finds no KIND_BLKDEV
  // entries, and returns 0 -- no side effects beyond the
  // PBP_ST_SCANNED counter staying at 0. probe_one_bdev is never
  // reached, so no BD_OP_READ_LBA (or the NVMEIO_PICK_NONE seam it
  // would traverse) is exercised on the substrate path.
  // ==========================================================================
  pub let pdxb_volume_probe_all_bdev : () -> u64 !{mem, sysreg} @{cap} =
    fn () -> unsafe {
      effects: {mem, sysreg},
      capabilities: {cap},
      justification: "R53.M3-002 (#1743): thin wrapper. Zero args, no register shuffling. sub rsp,8/add rsp,8 pad around the one nested call (even push count, 0) lands rsp%16==0 for the nested call per journal_ondisk.pdx's documented even/odd push-count rule -- same shape as jrp_ondisk_applied_count (journal_replay.pdx L592). rax already holds probe_all_bdevs's return value at ret. No test instruction, no branches, no reserved labels needed. The alias exists so kernel_main.pdx's wire-in matches the name pinned in the volume-lifecycle design doc (§4.1), keeping the boot-side call site independent of this module's internal loop-symbol name.",
      block: {
        sub rsp, 8;
        call probe_all_bdevs;
        add rsp, 8;
        ret
      }
    }
}
